1
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:34,990
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:37,910
[Episode 21]

3
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:17,690
I've been waiting for this day

4
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,010
for far too long.

5
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:26,310
God of Wealth.

6
00:03:31,690 --> 00:03:32,570
Du Huangqiao.

7
00:03:34,470 --> 00:03:38,070
You used to be a Nationalist Army
battalion commander yourself.

8
00:03:38,470 --> 00:03:39,710
We're no different—

9
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:43,130
risking our lives for others,

10
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,470
with no one coming to save us.

11
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:50,520
We've long been prepared
to die at any moment.

12
00:03:52,050 --> 00:03:53,930
You think you're so noble

13
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,560
and heroic, don't you?

14
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:01,770
Let me tell you something:

15
00:04:03,590 --> 00:04:05,800
I'm not going to let you die that easily.

16
00:04:07,770 --> 00:04:08,640
Otherwise,

17
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:12,190
how could I face Xiaoxian?

18
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:16,040
You were her best friend.

19
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:21,160
How could you bring yourself
to do that to her?

20
00:04:21,649 --> 00:04:24,050
You're the one
who drove her into a dead end.

21
00:04:26,150 --> 00:04:28,150
You used her to gather intelligence

22
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:31,220
and to fill the void in your heart.

23
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:34,480
You're the one who killed her.

24
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:36,200
Shut up!

25
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:46,070
Du Huangqiao.

26
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:48,870
In the end,

27
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:53,520
you're nothing but a dog for the Japanese—

28
00:04:53,890 --> 00:04:55,450
a stray, beaten-down dog.

29
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:59,960
No one would ever want
anything to do with the likes of you.

30
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:56,950
Jinbao. Jinbao!

31
00:06:59,310 --> 00:07:00,120
Xin Xiang!

32
00:07:02,010 --> 00:07:03,720
Xin Xiang, get the medical kit!

33
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,270
On it!

34
00:07:05,310 --> 00:07:06,000
Jinbao!

35
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,000
Jinbao!

36
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:09,920
Hurry! Gauze!

37
00:07:12,310 --> 00:07:13,910
Press it down. Press it down!

38
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,390
Gauze!

39
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,480
Jinbao. Jinbao!

40
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,390
Jinbao! Don't scare me!

41
00:07:34,310 --> 00:07:35,159
It itches.

42
00:07:35,659 --> 00:07:36,460
Don't do that.

43
00:07:40,110 --> 00:07:42,310
This won't do. We should go get a doctor.

44
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,920
No, let's go to the hospital.

45
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,310
Let's go, to the hospital!

46
00:07:45,310 --> 00:07:45,800
Let's go!

47
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,600
Don't move me!

48
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:53,320
I don't want to see a doctor at all
right now.

49
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,070
Not at all.

50
00:08:02,930 --> 00:08:04,130
Today is my birthday.

51
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,560
I just want to celebrate properly.

52
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:12,680
Okay.

53
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:14,920
Once you feel better,

54
00:08:15,270 --> 00:08:16,270
we'll celebrate.

55
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,200
I'm dying.

56
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:24,260
The doctors can't save me.

57
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,470
Just like this country—

58
00:08:31,070 --> 00:08:32,929
the doctors can't save it either.

59
00:08:37,669 --> 00:08:38,600
You can be saved.

60
00:08:39,630 --> 00:08:41,030
This country can be saved too.

61
00:08:41,030 --> 00:08:42,090
Both must be saved.

62
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,490
I don't want to go anywhere.

63
00:08:47,030 --> 00:08:48,510
I just want to stay here.

64
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:52,390
Okay.

65
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:54,440
Go, find a doctor.

66
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:54,910
Okay.

67
00:08:54,910 --> 00:08:56,710
Go! Hurry, find a doctor! Hurry!

68
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:08,700
While I still have my breath,

69
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,240
I want to have a proper talk with you.

70
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:22,240
There won't be another chance.

71
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,250
These past few days,

72
00:09:34,590 --> 00:09:36,390
I've been having the same dream—

73
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:40,510
about my childhood,

74
00:09:42,510 --> 00:09:43,200
Grandma,

75
00:09:44,390 --> 00:09:45,390
and Yinbao.

76
00:09:49,510 --> 00:09:51,000
Grandma raised us.

77
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,000
I'm going to find her.

78
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:03,510
I miss home.

79
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,720
I miss Yinbao.

80
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,870
I wonder how she's doing.

81
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,120
If you ever

82
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,790
see her someday,

83
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:26,790
remember to take good care of her for me.

84
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:30,540
Okay.

85
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,130
When you get better,

86
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,540
I'll take you home.

87
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,480
But I don't have a home.

88
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:48,840
My home is full of Japanese.

89
00:10:55,270 --> 00:10:56,240
Don't worry.

90
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:58,270
One day,

91
00:10:58,870 --> 00:11:00,270
we'll drive them all out.

92
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,510
My grandma said

93
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:08,980
I'm missing the "East" element
in my Five Elements,

94
00:11:10,390 --> 00:11:14,190
and that I'd be most compatible with
someone whose surname was Chen.

95
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:15,900
She was wrong about that.

96
00:11:19,170 --> 00:11:21,300
You're so cold-hearted and clueless.

97
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,770
You and I aren't compatible at all.

98
00:11:30,390 --> 00:11:31,920
But you must remember this:

99
00:11:35,510 --> 00:11:36,750
you're with the NBIS,

100
00:11:40,790 --> 00:11:42,600
and your mission isn't over yet.

101
00:11:47,730 --> 00:11:49,160
Okay, I know.

102
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,120
I got it.

103
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,550
Don't talk anymore. Stop talking.

104
00:11:51,550 --> 00:11:53,150
I know it all. I'll remember.

105
00:11:58,030 --> 00:11:59,430
Take a picture of me.

106
00:12:02,510 --> 00:12:03,960
Today's my birthday.

107
00:12:08,270 --> 00:12:10,730
I've always loved celebrating my birthday.

108
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:13,150
Okay.

109
00:12:13,630 --> 00:12:14,830
I'll take one for you.

110
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,200
My grandma used to say
that someone surnamed Chen and I

111
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:02,960
would make a great pair
when it came to making money.

112
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,540
You get all the benefits
and still complain.

113
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:05,720
All this misery, just because

114
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,250
I had a bowl of your wontons.

115
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,550
I'm telling you one last time:

116
00:14:08,550 --> 00:14:09,440
don't call me "Sis."

117
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:10,370
Sure thing, Sis.

118
00:14:10,870 --> 00:14:12,630
Then what else can I do to help you?

119
00:14:12,630 --> 00:14:13,750
I told you already,

120
00:14:13,870 --> 00:14:15,320
I don't need you to help me like this.

121
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:16,650
Before I change my mind,

122
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:17,910
hurry up and tell me.

123
00:14:17,910 --> 00:14:19,120
I'll never be able to pay you back.

124
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,550
I'd rather you owe me

125
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:22,840
than ignore me.

126
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:23,910
At least I know

127
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:26,960
you won't hurt me.

128
00:14:27,670 --> 00:14:28,790
Let's not cry.

129
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,660
Those of us who are still alive
have to live well.

130
00:15:05,130 --> 00:15:06,190
What are you doing?

131
00:15:08,750 --> 00:15:09,750
Taking pictures.

132
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,660
She's already dead.

133
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:31,180
What's there to take pictures of?

134
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:36,390
If I can take pictures of the living,

135
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,540
of course I can take pictures
of the dead too.

136
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,970
Was it you who brought her back?

137
00:15:57,150 --> 00:15:58,550
Was it you who killed her?

138
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:14,130
Do you know who she is?

139
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:19,750
Sh's the famous "God of Wealth"
of the NBIS.

140
00:16:25,790 --> 00:16:27,390
I don't care about the NBIS

141
00:16:28,180 --> 00:16:29,240
or "God of Wealth."

142
00:16:30,870 --> 00:16:32,670
All I know is that she's Jinbao.

143
00:16:35,030 --> 00:16:37,150
Auntie died at her hands.

144
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:39,270
I had to avenge her.

145
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:43,970
Didn't you say you wanted revenge
for Auntie too?

146
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:51,400
Jinbao

147
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,600
was family to me.

148
00:16:58,910 --> 00:16:59,750
Family?

149
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:05,270
Then what am I?

150
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:08,980
And what about Auntie?

151
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:12,000
Was it you who told this woman

152
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,599
that Auntie was still alive?

153
00:17:16,380 --> 00:17:17,140
I didn't.

154
00:17:24,839 --> 00:17:26,839
I really ought to put a bullet in you.

155
00:17:27,690 --> 00:17:28,339
Fine.

156
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,070
Then kill me.

157
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:46,380
You're nothing but an ant.

158
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:50,590
I can crush you anytime I want.

159
00:17:50,590 --> 00:17:51,400
Go ahead then!

160
00:17:52,590 --> 00:17:53,400
Kill me!

161
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,860
You kill me, and I'll kill you.

162
00:17:56,070 --> 00:17:58,000
Everyone around me is dead anyway.

163
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,720
Sooner or later, I'll die too!

164
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:01,350
Go ahead and kill me!

165
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:04,680
How many times have I told you?

166
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,200
Even if you pointed a gun at me,

167
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,830
I'd respect you more for it!

168
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,140
Where's the gun I gave you?

169
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:14,580
Where did it go?

170
00:18:21,030 --> 00:18:22,760
I'm not so cold-blooded as you.

171
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:27,830
Right now,

172
00:18:29,590 --> 00:18:31,590
I just want to live an ordinary life.

173
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:40,680
I just want my friends and family

174
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:45,200
to be able to live in peace and safety

175
00:18:46,030 --> 00:18:47,640
in this world.

176
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:04,640
I'll ask you one thing:

177
00:19:06,590 --> 00:19:09,590
what exactly is your relationship
with God of Wealth?

178
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,240
I don't care

179
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:18,360
what her identity is,

180
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:19,960
nor do I care.

181
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:24,240
But I like her.

182
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:27,720
What?

183
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,720
I said I like her!

184
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,160
So what?

185
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:36,400
Good.

186
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:40,640
You've finally made some progress.

187
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:33,780
[Fulai Photo Studio]

188
00:20:46,310 --> 00:20:47,030
I'm sorry.

189
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,560
I failed to protect your guest.

190
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:56,520
You took down the Hurricane Team
and God of Wealth.

191
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:59,350
I'd say that balances the scales.

192
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,480
I can offer you an official position

193
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:08,010
and let you stay with
the Plum Blossom Agency.

194
00:21:09,350 --> 00:21:10,880
I'm used to being free.

195
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:13,240
I don't like working a regular job.

196
00:21:13,550 --> 00:21:15,430
I just want to play
my three-stringed instrument

197
00:21:15,430 --> 00:21:17,230
and continue being the Cleaner.

198
00:21:22,110 --> 00:21:23,510
From now on,

199
00:21:24,830 --> 00:21:27,030
report any information directly to me.

200
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:30,010
Okay.

201
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:33,200
We still haven't dealt with

202
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,400
all the rats among us.

203
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:37,000
You promised me.

204
00:21:41,310 --> 00:21:42,880
I'll root them all out.

205
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:48,750
The research institute
has very strict security protocols.

206
00:21:48,750 --> 00:21:50,950
Hoshino is a man of forceful character,

207
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:54,980
and only researchers
are allowed into the laboratory.

208
00:21:57,270 --> 00:21:59,030
Without sufficient evidence,

209
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:03,200
you don't have the authority
to go in and investigate.

210
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:38,210
I'll kill Du Huangqiao.

211
00:22:41,310 --> 00:22:42,640
You're no match for him.

212
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:45,880
I have plenty of chances to kill him.

213
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:49,260
He's even more cunning

214
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:50,830
than you think.

215
00:22:58,240 --> 00:22:59,720
What were you thinking

216
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:02,770
when Zhao Qian died?

217
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:07,550
Same as you—

218
00:23:12,510 --> 00:23:14,770
thinking about how to kill Du Huangqiao.

219
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,310
Now that God of Wealth is gone,

220
00:23:56,310 --> 00:23:57,770
we'll bring in someone new

221
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,260
and get the codebook as soon as possible.

222
00:24:21,350 --> 00:24:22,200
Mr. Hoshino.

223
00:24:22,870 --> 00:24:23,730
Please come in.

224
00:24:31,350 --> 00:24:34,280
I brought the experimental materials
you asked for.

225
00:24:34,330 --> 00:24:35,460
Just put them there.

226
00:26:16,230 --> 00:26:17,270
This is Asami Sawa.

227
00:26:17,270 --> 00:26:18,130
Please come in.

228
00:26:20,450 --> 00:26:21,250
Excuse me.

229
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:27,200
Send these to Nanjing.

230
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:28,350
Got it.

231
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:32,960
I'll take my leave.

232
00:26:51,590 --> 00:26:53,320
You've all worked hard lately.

233
00:26:53,930 --> 00:26:57,580
The military police are holding
a Christmas party tonight.

234
00:26:58,720 --> 00:27:00,920
Since there will be a shuttle
to take us there,

235
00:27:00,920 --> 00:27:02,120
if anyone wants to go,

236
00:27:02,790 --> 00:27:04,070
just say so.

237
00:27:04,790 --> 00:27:05,480
I'll go.

238
00:27:05,510 --> 00:27:06,240
I want to go too.

239
00:27:06,240 --> 00:27:07,000
Count me in.

240
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:13,420
What are your plans, Mika? Are you going?

241
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:15,400
I'd like to get some proper rest.

242
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:17,950
I also have some files to sort out.

243
00:27:20,410 --> 00:27:22,760
Miss Mika really is hardworking.

244
00:27:27,720 --> 00:27:29,120
What about you, Yoshiko?

245
00:27:29,790 --> 00:27:33,270
I'd like to get some proper rest too.

246
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,480
Is that so?

247
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:40,160
What a shame.

248
00:27:41,070 --> 00:27:42,800
The guys in the military police

249
00:27:42,920 --> 00:27:44,880
will be really disappointed.

250
00:27:52,110 --> 00:27:53,590
What holiday is it today?

251
00:27:54,510 --> 00:27:55,590
Christmas Eve.

252
00:27:57,480 --> 00:27:59,920
What's Christmas Eve
supposed to celebrate?

253
00:27:59,920 --> 00:28:01,270
Probably

254
00:28:01,270 --> 00:28:03,200
peace and family reunion, I guess.

255
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:05,550
Have some tangyuan.

256
00:28:59,040 --> 00:28:59,970
As far as I know,

257
00:29:00,270 --> 00:29:02,870
there's an NBIS agent
hiding close to Hoshino.

258
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:04,550
He reports directly to Guan Yongshan,

259
00:29:04,550 --> 00:29:06,810
and only God of Wealth knew his identity.

260
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:09,720
He'll make your operation more difficult,

261
00:29:09,720 --> 00:29:11,160
but in an emergency,

262
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:13,210
you can also make use of him.

263
00:30:12,600 --> 00:30:13,540
Merry Christmas.

264
00:30:13,540 --> 00:30:14,540
Merry Christmas.

265
00:30:14,850 --> 00:30:16,190
Thank you for your hard work.

266
00:30:16,190 --> 00:30:16,920
Thank you.

267
00:30:17,300 --> 00:30:18,060
Thank you.

268
00:30:33,560 --> 00:30:35,080
In my hometown,

269
00:30:36,270 --> 00:30:39,960
it snows every Christmas.

270
00:30:42,830 --> 00:30:44,830
Snowfall is really beautiful.

271
00:30:48,510 --> 00:30:50,200
But it's not snowing.

272
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:10,400
Mr. Hoshino is back.

273
00:31:14,070 --> 00:31:15,400
It's getting a bit cold.

274
00:32:42,240 --> 00:32:44,240
You played that piece beautifully.

275
00:32:44,810 --> 00:32:46,470
Thank you for the compliment.

276
00:32:48,070 --> 00:32:49,510
It's Christmas today.

277
00:32:50,080 --> 00:32:51,810
Let's have some cake together.

278
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:55,160
Sure.

279
00:33:27,790 --> 00:33:28,650
Please come in.

280
00:33:29,350 --> 00:33:30,610
Let's eat in this room.

281
00:33:31,750 --> 00:33:33,110
I'll go make some tea.

282
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:30,510
Try it and see how you like it.

283
00:34:34,250 --> 00:34:36,080
Try that piano.

284
00:34:36,500 --> 00:34:37,190
Okay.

285
00:35:57,150 --> 00:35:57,880
Mr. Hoshino!

286
00:35:59,430 --> 00:36:00,180
Mr. Hoshino!

287
00:36:01,460 --> 00:36:02,190
Mr. Hoshino!

288
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:04,070
Someone!

289
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:06,360
Someone!

290
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:09,510
Someone!

291
00:36:09,840 --> 00:36:10,590
Someone!

292
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:11,760
Someone!

293
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:18,610
Mr. Hoshino!

294
00:36:19,280 --> 00:36:20,010
Mr. Hoshino!

295
00:36:20,670 --> 00:36:21,760
What happened?

296
00:36:22,590 --> 00:36:25,050
I don't know. It looks like
an asthma attack.

297
00:36:25,070 --> 00:36:27,800
Dr. Hoshino has a history of allergies.

298
00:36:28,190 --> 00:36:30,250
Did he come into contact with pollen?

299
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:31,960
No.

300
00:36:35,630 --> 00:36:37,280
He only drank matcha.

301
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:40,160
Hurry, get Mr. Hoshino to the hospital
right away!

302
00:36:53,570 --> 00:36:54,340
Mr. Hoshino!

303
00:36:58,110 --> 00:36:58,840
Mr. Hoshino!

304
00:38:17,150 --> 00:38:18,480
Put it in the trash can

305
00:38:18,480 --> 00:38:19,930
right across from the incinerator.

306
00:38:19,930 --> 00:38:21,710
The incinerator operator
checks it every day.

307
00:38:21,710 --> 00:38:22,710
He's one of us.

308
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:38,880
What's going on?

309
00:38:39,440 --> 00:38:40,030
Sir.

310
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:44,590
Dr. Hoshino suddenly went into
anaphylactic shock.

311
00:38:45,510 --> 00:38:46,510
Who did it?

312
00:38:47,710 --> 00:38:50,550
One of the assistants
caused it by accident.

313
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:53,880
I don't believe in accidents.

314
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:55,660
How's Dr. Hoshino now?

315
00:38:56,230 --> 00:38:57,590
He's recovering.

316
00:39:02,370 --> 00:39:03,630
I just saved your life,

317
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:05,810
and this is how you repay me?

318
00:39:05,810 --> 00:39:06,940
Who exactly are you?

319
00:39:08,920 --> 00:39:10,250
Who I am doesn't matter.

320
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:13,800
What matters is that
we share the same goal.

321
00:39:15,800 --> 00:39:18,000
You figured out who I was a long time ago?

322
00:39:20,320 --> 00:39:22,120
The callus on the web of your hand

323
00:39:22,850 --> 00:39:25,050
only comes from years of handling a gun.

324
00:39:26,590 --> 00:39:27,400
So,

325
00:39:28,440 --> 00:39:30,300
you deliberately covered for me?

326
00:39:33,510 --> 00:39:35,170
Can we talk in a different way?

327
00:39:43,070 --> 00:39:44,470
Thank you for helping me.

328
00:39:45,880 --> 00:39:46,810
You're welcome.

329
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:48,230
Like I said,

330
00:39:49,030 --> 00:39:50,400
we share the same goal.

331
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:53,610
You're a Communist?

332
00:40:01,030 --> 00:40:03,360
But you caused his allergic reaction
to pollen.

333
00:40:03,360 --> 00:40:04,440
He'll suspect you.

334
00:40:06,590 --> 00:40:07,760
I'm just an assistant

335
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:10,090
who didn't know about his pollen allergy.

336
00:40:10,590 --> 00:40:12,850
He won't necessarily give me a hard time.

337
00:40:13,760 --> 00:40:15,420
What are you planning to take?

338
00:40:17,230 --> 00:40:19,760
The research findings
from Project Slumber.

339
00:40:22,030 --> 00:40:24,430
The serum has already been sent
to Nanjing.

340
00:40:24,710 --> 00:40:26,000
As for the experiment report,

341
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:27,760
even if you get it, it won't help.

342
00:40:27,760 --> 00:40:29,960
Hoshino encrypts everything himself.

343
00:40:30,230 --> 00:40:32,690
It can only be deciphered
with the codebook.

344
00:40:34,150 --> 00:40:34,920
So you got it?

345
00:40:40,630 --> 00:40:42,490
How are you planning to get it out?

346
00:40:45,280 --> 00:40:47,480
I'm waiting for the right opportunity.

347
00:40:54,510 --> 00:40:55,840
If you trust me,

348
00:40:57,280 --> 00:40:58,880
I have a channel to get it out.

349
00:41:11,030 --> 00:41:11,830
Like you said,

350
00:41:12,920 --> 00:41:14,720
Hoshino is extremely paranoid.

351
00:41:15,190 --> 00:41:16,510
If the intelligence is in your possession

352
00:41:16,510 --> 00:41:17,970
and someone discovers it,

353
00:41:18,150 --> 00:41:19,950
none of us will make it out alive.

354
00:41:21,710 --> 00:41:22,640
Are you using me?

355
00:41:23,630 --> 00:41:24,760
If I were merely using you,

356
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:27,090
I wouldn't have risked my life
to save you.

357
00:41:27,480 --> 00:41:28,510
Stopping Project Slumber

358
00:41:28,510 --> 00:41:29,960
is a mission we all share.

359
00:41:31,150 --> 00:41:32,110
I promise you,

360
00:41:33,260 --> 00:41:35,520
once the intelligence has been sent out,

361
00:41:35,710 --> 00:41:37,710
I'll give you a copy of the codebook.

362
00:41:40,440 --> 00:41:42,500
Even if Hoshino starts to suspect me,

363
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:45,650
I'll still be able to get it out.

364
00:41:46,630 --> 00:41:48,160
For the sake of our country,

365
00:41:49,360 --> 00:41:50,490
we must stand united

366
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:52,490
at a time like this.

367
00:42:09,880 --> 00:42:10,650
I trust you.
